# Slice 346 (the book, colon-declares and forms-declare-or-call; the author 2026-11-10) and plan M11 5a (the author
# 2026-11-11): what declares and what writes. A place is declared by its receiver (`int: i 1`, `@: p main\data\Model`)
# and written by `:=`. A form `Name: tail` declares a Structure with the tail inside, its atoms not expanded: a path
# through an atom reaches the entity its word names -- Holder\Model is the Structure Model, one instance reached through
# Holder, through the reference p and by its own name; Pair\i is the place i, so a write through it is seen by i -- and
# an atom that names nothing stays a word (unknown_word). Declared again, Pair is one more occurrence of the name:
# main\data\[0]Pair has two fields, main\data\[1]Pair three; a bare Pair would be ambiguous.
# M11 5v: the Structures and their reference p live in own data; main() initializes p before the root's path writes.
# The code is explicitly empty. The atoms i and later name places of the root. The dump prints main as written
# (v 1); the live value 5 is read by through_model and through_ref.
sub: main () (
    Model:
        int: v 1
    @: p Model
    Holder: Model unknown_word
    Pair: a b
    Pair: i Model later
) ()
int: i 1
i := 6
int: i2 i + 1
main()
main\data\Holder\Model\v := 5
int: through_model main\data\Model\v
int: through_ref main\data\p\v
int: n_first length(main\data\[0]Pair)
int: n_second length(main\data\[1]Pair)
main\data\[1]Pair\i := 9
int: shared i
int: later 3
@: observed_p main\data\p
